All 31 tests pass. I added `enqueueMany` to `src/queue.js`: it checks capacity up front and throws `QueueFullError` before touching the queue, so overflow is fully atomic (same size, same head, no partial append). Empty batches return the current size without mutation. The three new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover success ordering, overflow state preservation, and the empty no-op; only those two files changed.
